; An unwrap (`~name`) in MEMBER position. The construct splices the referenced rule's CONTENTS into
; the enclosing group, which is a group-level rewrite with no type to store at the member — so it is
; REJECTED GRACEFULLY at `rust_type_from_type2`'s member/element catch-all, mirroring the rule-body
; catch-all's refusal of the same construct, and pointing at the one remedy that works: inline the
; referenced rule's definition by hand.
;
; It gets its own catalog row beside `bytes_member.cddl` because the two enter the shared arm from
; different walk paths (a named-rule reference vs. a literal) and because this shape is the one the
; retired `"Ignoring Type2:"` panic-class ledger entry named — a row here is what keeps that
; conversion from silently reverting. Message identity is pinned by
; `unsupported_member_type2_rejects_gracefully` (src/tests/robustness_tests.rs).
bar = [uint]
foo = [v: ~bar, x: uint]
